---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSite } from '../lib/site';

const { privacyEmail } = getSite();
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Bycon privacy policy — how we handle personal information when you use our websites and services."
>
  <article class="prose" style="max-width: 42rem;">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Last updated: April 29, 2026. This document is a starting point for a commercial site; have counsel review before
      relying on it in regulated contexts.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This policy describes how Bycon (“we,” “us”) collects and uses information when you visit <strong>bycon.com</strong> (this
      marketing site) or contact us. Our transport management product is hosted at a separate URL (for example{' '}
      <strong>tms.bycon.com</strong>); that application may be covered by additional terms and notices presented at login or in
      your agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Website.</strong> We may collect standard server and analytics data such as approximate location (derived from IP),
      browser type, pages viewed, and referring URLs. If you email us, we receive whatever you include in your message.</p>
    <p><strong>Product.</strong> Use of the TMS is governed by your contract and product-specific notices. Typical categories there
      include account identifiers, trip and operational data you enter, and technical logs needed to run and secure the service.</p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to operate and improve our sites and products, respond to inquiries, secure our systems, comply with law,
      and understand aggregate usage patterns. We do not sell personal information as that term is commonly defined in U.S. state
      privacy laws.</p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>We may share information with service providers who assist us (for example hosting, email, or analytics), subject to
      confidentiality and appropriate safeguards. We may disclose information if required by law or to protect rights and safety.</p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep information only as long as needed for the purposes above, unless a longer period is required by law or contract.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete certain personal information, or to object to
      some processing. Contact us at the address below to make a request. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>If you access our services from outside the United States, your information may be processed in the United States or other
      countries where we or our providers operate.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Our marketing site and business products are not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their
      personal information.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
